> since make four-leaf clovers with my god and the problem stopped.
> Despite this I insist that this is a bug since its unfair to
> effectively disable searching.Searching is critical to progress and
> breaking searches is unfair. It's ok for troubled characters to have a
> penalty but 400 turns goes too far..

Well, every 600 turns your luck will increase if it's negative--unless
you're carrying a non-blessed luckstone, in which case bad luck does
not time out.  So unless you carry a luckstone, the penalties won't
last very long--and that still makes a luckstone far less of a penalty
than a loadstone or other objects.

I guess the non-obvious thing is that unicorns are important luck
totems, and they're important to your god.  But learning that is a part
of the game.

The other ways to get massive luck penalties is to do stuff that seems
pretty deserving of penalties (cannibalism, praying at altars to other
gods, sacrificing your own race, etc) or to repeatedly violate smaller
rules (particularly, Sokoban rules or breaking mirrors).



